    "provider": "ICAS",
    "q": "<figure class=\"aa-source workshop-facsimile\"><img class=\"source-facsimile\" src=\"assets/arp-workshop-additions/ws-source-059.png\" width=\"1728\" height=\"972\" alt=\"Question 1\nWhat will an entity need to disclose to allow users to assess how well \nthey have engaged with stakeholders?  \n \nICAS ARP Workshop 3\n13\" loading=\"eager\"></figure>",
    "a": "<figure class=\"aa-source workshop-facsimile\"><img class=\"source-facsimile\" src=\"assets/arp-workshop-additions/ws-source-060.png\" width=\"1728\" height=\"972\" alt=\"Question 1 – Answer \nTo enable the stakeholder engagement process to be assessed, entities \nshould disclose:\n• the criteria for determining their stakeholder groups and who those \ngroups are\n• the method and frequency of engagement, on an ongoing basis and \nfor determining material topics\n• the views and concerns of stakeholders by group\n• how stakeholder feedback influenced the selection, review and \nupdating of material topics.\nICAS ARP Workshop 3\n14\" loading=\"eager\"></figure>",
    "searchText": "Question 1\nWhat will an entity need to disclose to allow users to assess how well \nthey have engaged with stakeholders?  \n \nICAS ARP Workshop 3\n13",
    "isHTML": true,
    "workshopOrigin": "slides",
    "sourceFiles": [
      "sources/ARP Workshop 3 - 5pm slides.pdf"
    ],
    "linkTags": [
      "stakeholder-engagement"
    ],
    "lesson": "Lesson2",
    "assessmentApproach": {
      "title": "Assessment technique · source slides",
      "html": "<figure class=\"aa-source workshop-facsimile\"><img class=\"source-facsimile\" src=\"assets/arp-workshop-additions/ws-source-087.png\" width=\"1728\" height=\"972\" alt=\"Assessment technique \n•\nRead the questions before you start working  \n•\nDo what is required – Advise, explain, calculate, prepare journals, construct, analyse, \nevaluate, recommend. \n•\nAdvise – What relevant standards apply to the information in the question and what \ndoes this mean for the company;   eg. advise how revenue should be accounted for.  \n•\nAnalyse – Use information to come to a conclusion eg. advise if a contract is a lease.\n•\nEvaluate – Compare what has been done against what should have been done eg. \nevaluate the extent to which disclosures comply with relevant standards.  \n•\nRecommend – how can any gaps be dealt with eg. recommend two improvements to \nexisting disclosures.\n•\nBe clear and concise in your response – do not talk around the issue but fail to \naddress the point; reference standards and how they apply/do not apply to the scenario\nICAS ARP Workshop 3\n84\" loading=\"eager\"></figure><figure class=\"aa-source workshop-facsimile\"><img class=\"source-facsimile\" src=\"assets/arp-workshop-additions/ws-source-088.png\" width=\"1728\" height=\"972\" alt=\"Assessment technique \nTUTOR TIPS: \n•\nAssessment marks will be ROUGHLY split 50:50 for explanations and \ncalculations / presentation / disclosures… be ready to write, not just calculate\n•\nBe specific in your answers in relation to the scenario, you must be applying \nknowledge and your explanations to facts and details in the scenario in the \nquestion.\n•\nTo study for the assessment: Question practice is key! Practice your \nexplanations and advise requirements, this is a key skill at ARP! \n•\nComplete question practice using assessment timings and where possible under \nassessment conditions without your notes.\n•\nUtilise your permitted materials and practice using them whilst doing your \nquestion practice.\nICAS ARP Workshop 3\n85\" loading=\"eager\"></figure>"
    },
    "tutorTips": {
      "title": "Non-financial disclosures · tutor tips",
      "html": "<figure class=\"aa-source workshop-facsimile\"><img class=\"source-facsimile\" src=\"assets/arp-workshop-additions/ws-source-092.png\" width=\"1728\" height=\"972\" alt=\"Non-financial disclosures – tutor tips \n• You may be expected to evaluate the adequacy of disclosures and make recommendations for \nimprovements to draft disclosures that have been prepared by the reporting entity.\n• You could be asked whether information prepared under one set of standards is more useful, or \nprovides better quality information, to stakeholders. The ability to assess whether information \nmeets the reporting principles of the standard, including through the requirement / lack of \nrequirement for external assurance, is an important consideration when considering the \nusefulness and quality of information.\n• You are expected to have a high-level understanding of the requirements of the relevant \nstandards relating to climate-related issues, the approach to Governance and materiality, but \nnot the specific details and references. \n• You may be provided with a short extract from a specific standard in the assessment which you \nneed to apply to the scenario given.\nICAS ARP Workshop 3\n21\" loading=\"eager\"></figure><figure class=\"aa-source workshop-facsimile\"><img class=\"source-facsimile\" src=\"assets/arp-workshop-additions/ws-source-093.png\" width=\"1728\" height=\"972\" alt=\"Non-financial disclosures – tutor tips \n▪You won’t be expected to advise on climate-related risks and opportunities for different \nindustries, however, you could be provided with a scenario to analyse with a requirement to: \n• identify the risks and opportunities described\n• categorise risks into physical and transition risks \n• identify the financial impact of climate-related risks and opportunities for a particular entity. \n▪When considering the strategic report, you do not need to memorise the definitions of a small \ncompany or micro-entity. You will be provided with extracts from the Companies Act 2006 where \nthey are required. \n• You need to be able to apply those definitions to the scenario to determine whether a \ncompany is a small company or micro-entity.\nICAS ARP Workshop 3\n22\" loading=\"eager\"></figure><figure class=\"aa-source workshop-facsimile\"><img class=\"source-facsimile\" src=\"assets/arp-workshop-additions/ws-source-094.png\" width=\"1728\" height=\"972\" alt=\"Non-financial disclosures – tutor tips \n•You may be asked to evaluate financial and non-financial disclosures to \ndetermine whether they are consistent. The main areas of consistency and \ninconsistency should be applied in the context of the scenario given.\n•You may be asked whether climate-related matters should be taken into account \nwhen preparing financial statements. The scenarios will be limited to the IFRS \nAccounting Standards covered previously.\nICAS ARP Workshop 3\n23\" loading=\"eager\"></figure>"
    },
