    "q": "<figure class=\"aa-source workshop-facsimile\"><img class=\"source-facsimile\" src=\"assets/arp-workshop-additions/ws-source-061.png\" width=\"1728\" height=\"972\" alt=\"Question 2\nWhat are the three sections which a company has to include in its \nstrategic report?\n \nICAS ARP Workshop 3\n15\" loading=\"eager\"></figure>",
    "a": "<figure class=\"aa-source workshop-facsimile\"><img class=\"source-facsimile\" src=\"assets/arp-workshop-additions/ws-source-062.png\" width=\"1728\" height=\"972\" alt=\"Question 2 – Answer\n•Strategic management – an explanation of the company’s strategy, objectives \nand business model.\n•The Business environment in which the company operates, including the \nprincipal risks and uncertainties facing the business, changes in the \nmarketplace, and relevant environmental and social matters.\n•Business position and performance – an analysis of the entity’s performance, \nincluding appropriate qualitative and quantitative information, with appropriate \nreference to key performance indicators (KPIs).\nICAS ARP Workshop 3\n16\" loading=\"eager\"></figure>",
