    "provider": "ICAS",
    "q": "<figure class=\"aa-source workshop-facsimile\"><img class=\"source-facsimile\" src=\"assets/arp-workshop-additions/ws-source-074.png\" width=\"1728\" height=\"972\" alt=\"Equity Settled Share Based Payments\nVesting Conditions Question: Berry plc\nBerry plc (Berry) has granted share options to its 1,000 employees on the following\nbasis:\n• Each employee will be entitled to 500 options if they remain with Berry for the three years from 1 \nJanuary 20X1\n• At the grant date, each option is estimated to have a fair value of £3.50\n• At the year ended 31 December 20X1, 50 staff leave and Berry estimates a total of 100 will leave \nover the two years from 1 January 20X2\n• During 20X2, 60 staff leave and it is now estimated that 55 will leave in 20X3\n• During 20X3, 45 staff leave\n1. Calculate providing explanations and showing all workings, the amounts that should \nappear in the financial statements for the years ended 31 December 20X1, 20X2 and 20X3.\n2. Prepare the journal entry to account for the share-based payment for the year ended 31 \nDecember 20X3.\nICAS ARP Workshop 3\n48\" loading=\"eager\"></figure>",
    "a": "<figure class=\"aa-source workshop-facsimile\"><img class=\"source-facsimile\" src=\"assets/arp-workshop-additions/ws-source-075.png\" width=\"1728\" height=\"972\" alt=\"Equity Settled Share Based Payments\n• Solution: Berry plc\n• There is a three-year service condition and the options relate to services provided by the employees over \nthat three-year period.\n• The cost of these services should be recognised over the three years and the number of options expected to \nvest revised annually, based on changes to eligible staff.\n• The transaction is measured using the fair value at the grant date. The fair value is not revised.\nICAS ARP Workshop 3\n49\nExpense £000\nEquity £000\n31 December 20X1\n(1,000 – 50 -100) employees x \n500 options x £3.50 x 1/3 years\n496\n496\n31 December 20X2\n(1,000 – 50 – 60 - 55) employees \nx 500 options x £3.50 x 2/3 years \n- £496k\n478\n974\n31 December 20X3\n(1,000 – 50 – 60 - 45) employees \nx 500 options x £3.50 x 3/3 years \n- £974k\n505\n1,479\" loading=\"eager\"></figure><figure class=\"aa-source workshop-facsimile\"><img class=\"source-facsimile\" src=\"assets/arp-workshop-additions/ws-source-076.png\" width=\"1728\" height=\"972\" alt=\"Equity Settled Share Based Payments\nSolution: Berry plc\nJournal Entry\nICAS ARP Workshop 3\n50\n£000\n£000\nDr SPL – staff costs\n505\nCr Retained Earnings\n505\nbeing share-based payment expense for the year ended 31 December 20X3\" loading=\"eager\"></figure>",
    "searchText": "Equity Settled Share Based Payments\nVesting Conditions Question: Berry plc\nBerry plc (Berry) has granted share options to its 1,000 employees on the following\nbasis:\n• Each employee will be entitled to 500 options if they remain with Berry for the three years from 1 \nJanuary 20X1\n• At the grant date, each option is estimated to have a fair value of £3.50\n• At the year ended 31 December 20X1, 50 staff leave and Berry estimates a total of 100 will leave \nover the two years from 1 January 20X2\n• During 20X2, 60 staff leave and it is now estimated that 55 will leave in 20X3\n• During 20X3, 45 staff leave\n1. Calculate providing explanations and showing all workings, the amounts that should \nappear in the financial statements for the years ended 31 December 20X1, 20X2 and 20X3.\n2. Prepare the journal entry to account for the share-based payment for the year ended 31 \nDecember 20X3.\nICAS ARP Workshop 3\n48",
