    "q": "<figure class=\"aa-source workshop-facsimile\"><img class=\"source-facsimile\" src=\"assets/arp-workshop-additions/ws-source-077.png\" width=\"1728\" height=\"972\" alt=\"Cash-Settled Shared-based payments\n• What are they used for?\n• How are they measured\n• When and how are they recognised\n• How do the following terms apply:\n• Grant date\n• Vest date\n• Vesting period\n• Conditions?\n• What happens at subsequent reporting dates\n \nICAS ARP Workshop 3\n51\" loading=\"eager\"></figure>",
    "a": "<figure class=\"aa-source workshop-facsimile\"><img class=\"source-facsimile\" src=\"assets/arp-workshop-additions/ws-source-078.png\" width=\"1728\" height=\"972\" alt=\"Cash-Settled Share-Based Payments\n•\nCash-settled share-based payments are usually a form of reward provided to employees in \nexchange for their services. They may take the form of:\n•\nShare appreciation rights (SARs), which grant employees a right to a future cash \npayment that is based on an increase in share price over a defined period\n•\nA right to shares that are redeemable (not examinable in ARP)\n•\nRecognise at FV of the liability when the goods or service are provided\nDr Expense or Asset / Cr  Liability (Other payables) \n•\nA cash-settled transaction is recognised in the same way as an equity-settled transaction (i.e. \nover the vesting period). BUT, we will update the fair value at each reporting date. \n•\nAny remeasurement gains or losses are recognised in profit or loss, including when the \nshare-based payment qualifies for recognition as an asset.\n•\nAt vest date DR Liability (Other payables) / CR Bank\nICAS ARP Workshop 3\n52\" loading=\"eager\"></figure>",
    "searchText": "Cash-Settled Shared-based payments\n• What are they used for?\n• How are they measured\n• When and how are they recognised\n• How do the following terms apply:\n• Grant date\n• Vest date\n• Vesting period\n• Conditions?\n• What happens at subsequent reporting dates\n \nICAS ARP Workshop 3\n51",
