    "provider": "ICAS",
    "q": "<figure class=\"aa-source workshop-facsimile\"><img class=\"source-facsimile\" src=\"assets/arp-workshop-additions/ws-source-079.png\" width=\"1728\" height=\"972\" alt=\"Cash Settled Share Based Payments\nVesting Conditions Question: Eammon plc\nEammon plc (Eammon) grants 500 SAR to each of its 300 employees on 1 January 20X1, on the \ncondition that the employees remain with the company for the next two years.\n• The SAR must be exercised on 1 January 20X3.\n• At 31 December 20X1, the best estimate was that 80% of the staff qualified for the scheme. At \nthe end of 20X2, the best estimate was that 82% of staff qualified for the scheme.\n• The estimates for the fair value of each SAR at the end of each year are as follows:\n1. Prepare, showing all workings, journal entries to account for the share-based\npayment arrangement for the years ended 31 December 20X1, 20X2 and 20X3.\nICAS ARP Workshop 3\n53\n20X1\n£12.00\n20X2\n£14.30\" loading=\"eager\"></figure>",
    "a": "<figure class=\"aa-source workshop-facsimile\"><img class=\"source-facsimile\" src=\"assets/arp-workshop-additions/ws-source-080.png\" width=\"1728\" height=\"972\" alt=\"Cash Settled Share Based Payments\nSolution: Eammon plc\nICAS ARP Workshop 3\n54\nExpense £000\nLiability £000\n31 December \n20X1\n(80% x 300 employees) x 500 \nSAR x £12.00 x 1/2\nyears\n720\n720\n31 December \n20X2\n([82% x 300 employees] x 500 \nSAR x £14.30) - £720k\n1,039\n1,759\" loading=\"eager\"></figure><figure class=\"aa-source workshop-facsimile\"><img class=\"source-facsimile\" src=\"assets/arp-workshop-additions/ws-source-081.png\" width=\"1728\" height=\"972\" alt=\"Cash Settled Share Based Payments\nSolution: Eammon plc\nJournal Entry\nICAS ARP Workshop 3\n55\n£000\n£000\nDr SPL – staff costs\n720\nCr Other payables\n720\nbeing share-based payment expense for the year ended 31 December 20X1\n£000\n£000\nDr SPL – staff costs\n1,039\nCr Other payables\n1,039\nbeing share-based payment expense for the year ended 31 December 20X2\" loading=\"eager\"></figure><figure class=\"aa-source workshop-facsimile\"><img class=\"source-facsimile\" src=\"assets/arp-workshop-additions/ws-source-082.png\" width=\"1728\" height=\"972\" alt=\"Cash Settled Share Based Payments\nSolution: Eammon plc\nJournal Entry\nICAS ARP Workshop 3\n56\n£000\n£000\nDr Other Payables\n1,759\nCr Bank\n1,759\nbeing settlement of share-based payment liability on 1 January 20X3\" loading=\"eager\"></figure>",
    "searchText": "Cash Settled Share Based Payments\nVesting Conditions Question: Eammon plc\nEammon plc (Eammon) grants 500 SAR to each of its 300 employees on 1 January 20X1, on the \ncondition that the employees remain with the company for the next two years.\n• The SAR must be exercised on 1 January 20X3.\n• At 31 December 20X1, the best estimate was that 80% of the staff qualified for the scheme. At \nthe end of 20X2, the best estimate was that 82% of staff qualified for the scheme.\n• The estimates for the fair value of each SAR at the end of each year are as follows:\n1. Prepare, showing all workings, journal entries to account for the share-based\npayment arrangement for the years ended 31 December 20X1, 20X2 and 20X3.\nICAS ARP Workshop 3\n53\n20X1\n£12.00\n20X2\n£14.30",
