      "html": "<figure class=\"aa-source workshop-facsimile\"><img class=\"source-facsimile\" src=\"assets/arp-workshop-additions/ws-source-087.png\" width=\"1728\" height=\"972\" alt=\"Assessment technique \n•\nRead the questions before you start working  \n•\nDo what is required – Advise, explain, calculate, prepare journals, construct, analyse, \nevaluate, recommend. \n•\nAdvise – What relevant standards apply to the information in the question and what \ndoes this mean for the company;   eg. advise how revenue should be accounted for.  \n•\nAnalyse – Use information to come to a conclusion eg. advise if a contract is a lease.\n•\nEvaluate – Compare what has been done against what should have been done eg. \nevaluate the extent to which disclosures comply with relevant standards.  \n•\nRecommend – how can any gaps be dealt with eg. recommend two improvements to \nexisting disclosures.\n•\nBe clear and concise in your response – do not talk around the issue but fail to \naddress the point; reference standards and how they apply/do not apply to the scenario\nICAS ARP Workshop 3\n84\" loading=\"eager\"></figure><figure class=\"aa-source workshop-facsimile\"><img class=\"source-facsimile\" src=\"assets/arp-workshop-additions/ws-source-088.png\" width=\"1728\" height=\"972\" alt=\"Assessment technique \nTUTOR TIPS: \n•\nAssessment marks will be ROUGHLY split 50:50 for explanations and \ncalculations / presentation / disclosures… be ready to write, not just calculate\n•\nBe specific in your answers in relation to the scenario, you must be applying \nknowledge and your explanations to facts and details in the scenario in the \nquestion.\n•\nTo study for the assessment: Question practice is key! Practice your \nexplanations and advise requirements, this is a key skill at ARP! \n•\nComplete question practice using assessment timings and where possible under \nassessment conditions without your notes.\n•\nUtilise your permitted materials and practice using them whilst doing your \nquestion practice.\nICAS ARP Workshop 3\n85\" loading=\"eager\"></figure>"
